course: dictionary
lesson: 10698
title: Unsecured: not fixed, not locked, not backed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Small pets left in unsecured runs can be caught by foxes, cats, dogs or birds.» Look at the words around unsecured. The pets can be caught by foxes and cats, so the run must be open to them. The clue tells you it means not protected.
explain: The word has three parts: un- means not, and secure means safe or firmly fixed. So unsecured means not made safe or not fixed firmly. Check it: «Small pets left in runs that are not protected can be caught by foxes» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: The same word can be used in different places. A box in a car that is not fixed down is unsecured. A Wi-Fi network with no password is unsecured. A loan that is not backed by a house or other property is also unsecured. In each case, the word means something is not protected or fixed firmly.
fact: Unsecured means not fixed or fastened firmly, so it can move or fall.
fact: «Unsecured» can also mean not locked or protected, so other people can get in.
fact: An unsecured loan is a loan that is not backed by a house or other property.
fact: Look for clues in the sentence: if something could be stolen, hurt someone or fall, the word probably means not protected or not fixed.
fact: Un- at the start of a word often means not, as in unlocked, unsafe and unfair.
exercise: «Small pets left in unsecured runs can be caught by foxes, cats, dogs or birds.» What does unsecured mean here? | *Not locked or protected, so animals can get in | Fixed to the ground with a chain | Very tidy and clean | Made of strong metal
exercise: A ladder is unsecured if it is: | Covered with a password | Locked with a key | Made of wood | *Not fixed firmly, so it could fall
exercise: An unsecured Wi-Fi network means: | *Anyone can join it, because it has no password | It is only for the school | Nobody can see it at all | It is very fast
test: What does an unsecured load in a car mean? | A load that is locked in with a key | A load that is too small to see | *A load that is not fixed down and could fall or move | A load of shopping
test: An unsecured loan is one that is: | *Not backed by a house or other property | Given to children for free | Paid back every week by a bank | Backed by a house
exam: Which sentence shows an unsecured ladder? | The ladder was fixed firmly to the wall | *The ladder wobbled and was not fixed, so it could fall | The ladder was made of wood | The ladder was painted green
